Ji\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01DnFmHfu16x1qXKHUDXPpgX\":{\"file_path\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/friendly_document-new-optional-api-env-vars/brief.md\"}}}\n4\t{\"type\":\"rate_limit_event\",\"rate_limit_info\":{\"status\":\"allowed\",\"resetsAt\":1792017000,\"rateLimitType\":\"five_hour\",\"overageStatus\":\"rejected\",\"overageDisabledReason\":\"org_level_disabled\",\"isUsingOverage\":false,\"unifiedWindows\":{\"five_hour\":{\"utilization\":0.35,\"resetsAt\":1792017000},\"seven_day\":{\"utilization\":0.42,\"resetsAt\":1792198800}}},\"uuid\":\"b311b989-6ce8-48df-b5a1-f68dd0cc49a0\",\"session_id\":\"f3d69f9c-a2d3-42af-8038-53845031b34c\"}\n5\t{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01DnFmHfu16x1qXKHUDXPpgX\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t# Brief: document new optional API env vars\\n2\\t\\n3\\ttype: feature\\n4\\tid: friendly\\n5\\tbranch: feature/friendly_document-new-optional-api-env-vars\\n6\\tdate: 2026-10-14\\n7\\tauthor: Leander Muskalla\\n8\\t\\n9\\t## What\\n10\\t\\n11\\tExpose the new optional settings from solyto/api in `.env` and `README.md`:\\n12\\t\\n13\\t- `MIN_CLIENT_VERSION` (`c5f3b99`): authenticated requests whose\\n14\\t  `X-Client-Version` header is below this version get a 426. Requests without\\n15\\t  the header are always allowed. Empty/unset turns the check off.\\n16\\t- `API_TRAFFIC_ALERT_THRESHOLD` (default `300`) and\\n17\\t  `API_TRAFFIC_ALERT_COOLDOWN` (default `3600` seconds) (`fb9b5d1`): alert\\n18\\t  admins when a single user sends too many API requests.\\n19\\t\\n20\\t## Why\\n21\\t\\n22\\tAll three have safe defaults, so nothing breaks without them. But\\n23\\tself-hosters can't tune them if they don't know they exist.\\n24\\t\\n25\\t## Decisions\\n26\\t\\n27\\t- Undecided: add them to `.env` (commented out or with defaults), or only\\n28\\t  mention them in `README.md`.\\n29\\t\\n30\\t## Out of scope\\n31\\t\\n32\\t- Changing defaults.\\n33\\t\\n34\\t## Notes\\n35\\t\\n36\\t- Not verified: whether traffic alerts go out via ntfy (they likely use the\\n37\\t  new admin notifications, see `ntfy-notifications.md`). The API also logs\\n38\\t  them to `storage/logs/traffic.log`. Check before documenting.\\n39\\t\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f3d69f9c-a2d3-42af-8038-53845031b34c\",\"uuid\":\"3d9b6505-9139-485e-a216-5a752935db66\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-14T20:33:50.234Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/friendly_document-new-optional-api-env-vars/brief.md\",\"content\":\"# Brief: document new optional API env vars\\n\\ntype: feature\\nid: friendly\\nbranch: feature/friendly_document-new-optional-api-env-vars\\ndate: 2026-10-14\\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\\n\\n## What\\n\\nExpose the new optional settings from solyto/api in `.env` and `README.md`:\\n\\n- `MIN_CLIENT_VERSION` (`c5f3b99`): authenticated requests whose\\n  `X-Client-Version` header is below this version get a 426. Requests without\\n  the header are always allowed. Empty/unset turns the check off.\\n- `API_TRAFFIC_ALERT_THRESHOLD` (default `300`) and\\n  `API_TRAFFIC_ALERT_COOLDOWN` (default `3600` seconds) (`fb9b5d1`): alert\\n  admins when a single user sends too many API requests.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nAll three have safe defaults, so nothing breaks without them. But\\nself-hosters can't tune them if they don't know they exist.\\n\\n## Decisions\\n\\n- Undecided: add them to `.env` (commented out or with defaults), or only\\n  mention them in `README.md`.\\n\\n## Out of scope\\n\\n- Changing defaults.\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\n- Not verified: whether traffic alerts go out via ntfy (they likely use the\\n  new admin notifications, see `ntfy-notifications.md`). The API also logs\\n  them to `storage/logs/traffic.log`. Check before documenting.\\n\",\"numLines\":39,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":39}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01DnFmHfu16x1qXKHUDXPpgX\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\