{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sqb84bRKZEQcVoGPmqKPWY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Backlog: document new optional API env vars\n2\t\n3\tcreated: 2026-10-14\n4\t\n5\t## What\n6\t\n7\tExpose the new optional settings from solyto/api in `.env` and `README.md`:\n8\t\n9\t- `MIN_CLIENT_VERSION` (`c5f3b99`): authenticated requests whose\n10\t  `X-Client-Version` header is below this version get a 426. Requests without\n11\t  the header are always allowed. Empty/unset turns the check off.\n12\t- `API_TRAFFIC_ALERT_THRESHOLD` (default `300`) and\n13\t  `API_TRAFFIC_ALERT_COOLDOWN` (default `3600` seconds) (`fb9b5d1`): alert\n14\t  admins when a single user sends too many API requests.\n15\t\n16\t## Why\n17\t\n18\tAll three have safe defaults, so nothing breaks without them. But\n19\tself-hosters can't tune them if they don't know they exist.\n20\t\n21\t## Decisions\n22\t\n23\t- Undecided: add them to `.env` (commented out or with defaults), or only\n24\t  mention them in `README.md`.\n25\t\n26\t## Out of scope\n27\t\n28\t- Changing defaults.\n29\t\n30\t## Notes\n31\t\n32\t- Not verified: whether traffic alerts go out via ntfy (they likely use the\n33\t  new admin notifications, see `ntfy-notifications.md`). The API also logs\n34\t  them to `storage/logs/traffic.log`. Check before documenting.\n35\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3d69f9c-a2d3-42af-8038-53845031b34c","uuid":"44a5c63b-ea1e-43b2-8ce9-0f6836be13cb","timestamp":"2026-10-14T20:34:00.159Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/backlog/optional-api-env-vars.md","content":"# Backlog: document new optional API env vars\n\ncreated: 2026-10-14\n\n## What\n\nExpose the new optional settings from solyto/api in `.env` and `README.md`:\n\n- `MIN_CLIENT_VERSION` (`c5f3b99`): authenticated requests whose\n  `X-Client-Version` header is below this version get a 426. Requests without\n  the header are always allowed. Empty/unset turns the check off.\n- `API_TRAFFIC_ALERT_THRESHOLD` (default `300`) and\n  `API_TRAFFIC_ALERT_COOLDOWN` (default `3600` seconds) (`fb9b5d1`): alert\n  admins when a single user sends too many API requests.\n\n## Why\n\nAll three have safe defaults, so nothing breaks without them. But\nself-hosters can't tune them if they don't know they exist.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- Undecided: add them to `.env` (commented out or with defaults), or only\n  mention them in `README.md`.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Changing defaults.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Not verified: whether traffic alerts go out via ntfy (they likely use the\n  new admin notifications, see `ntfy-notifications.md`). The API also logs\n  them to `storage/logs/traffic.log`. Check before documenting.\n","numLines":35,"startLine":1,"totalLines":35}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Sqb84bRKZEQcVoGPmqKPWY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
