{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SdQ1JYW8TyySA3oa192dHX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Backlog: ntfy notifications for instance admins\n2\t\n3\tcreated: 2026-10-14\n4\t\n5\t## What\n6\t\n7\tWire up the ntfy admin notifications added in solyto/api (`337a3e1`) for\n8\tself-hosters:\n9\t\n10\t- `compose.yml`: top-level secrets `ntfy_topic` and `ntfy_token`. On `api` and\n11\t  `queue`, add `NTFY_TOPIC_FILE=/run/secrets/ntfy_topic`,\n12\t  `NTFY_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/ntfy_token` and the service-level `secrets:`\n13\t  entries.\n14\t- `setup.sh`: add `write_empty \"ntfy_topic\"` and `write_empty \"ntfy_token\"` to\n15\t  the optional secrets.\n16\t- `.env`: `NTFY_URL=` (empty) in its own block.\n17\t- `README.md`: list `ntfy_topic` and `ntfy_token` under optional secrets and\n18\t  note that ntfy is off unless URL and topic are both set.\n19\t\n20\t## Why\n21\t\n22\tThe API now reads `NTFY_URL` from env and `NTFY_TOPIC` / `NTFY_TOKEN` via\n23\t`DockerSecretHelper`. Without these changes self-hosters can't enable it.\n24\t\n25\t## Decisions\n26\t\n27\t- Secrets go on `api` and `queue` only (`api` evaluates `via()`, `queue`\n28\t  sends). `dav`, `nginx` and `imgproxy` need nothing.\n29\t- No defaults and no fallback to ntfy.sh: an instance makes no outbound call\n30\t  unless the operator sets URL and topic.\n31\t\n32\t## Out of scope\n33\t\n34\t- Any change to the API itself.\n35\t\n36\t## Notes\n37\t\n38\t- The `write_empty` entries are required: compose fails on a missing secret\n39\t  file. An empty file is fine, the API checks with `filled()`.\n40\t- Existing installs need to create the two secret files manually (or rerun the\n41\t  relevant part of `setup.sh`) before pulling the new `compose.yml`.\n42\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3d69f9c-a2d3-42af-8038-53845031b34c","uuid":"5cf04590-02eb-4339-9bf6-40b2d4642e50","timestamp":"2026-10-14T20:34:00.312Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/backlog/ntfy-notifications.md","content":"# Backlog: ntfy notifications for instance admins\n\ncreated: 2026-10-14\n\n## What\n\nWire up the ntfy admin notifications added in solyto/api (`337a3e1`) for\nself-hosters:\n\n- `compose.yml`: top-level secrets `ntfy_topic` and `ntfy_token`. On `api` and\n  `queue`, add `NTFY_TOPIC_FILE=/run/secrets/ntfy_topic`,\n  `NTFY_TOKEN_FILE=/run/secrets/ntfy_token` and the service-level `secrets:`\n  entries.\n- `setup.sh`: add `write_empty \"ntfy_topic\"` and `write_empty \"ntfy_token\"` to\n  the optional secrets.\n- `.env`: `NTFY_URL=` (empty) in its own block.\n- `README.md`: list `ntfy_topic` and `ntfy_token` under optional secrets and\n  note that ntfy is off unless URL and topic are both set.\n\n## Why\n\nThe API now reads `NTFY_URL` from env and `NTFY_TOPIC` / `NTFY_TOKEN` via\n`DockerSecretHelper`. Without these changes self-hosters can't enable it.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- Secrets go on `api` and `queue` only (`api` evaluates `via()`, `queue`\n  sends). `dav`, `nginx` and `imgproxy` need nothing.\n- No defaults and no fallback to ntfy.sh: an instance makes no outbound call\n  unless the operator sets URL and topic.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Any change to the API itself.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The `write_empty` entries are required: compose fails on a missing secret\n  file. An empty file is fine, the API checks with `filled()`.\n- Existing installs need to create the two secret files manually (or rerun the\n  relevant part of `setup.sh`) before pulling the new `compose.yml`.\n","numLines":42,"startLine":1,"totalLines":42}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SdQ1JYW8TyySA3oa192dHX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
