{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0125UjFUF2ygL5m93Dgy46DT","type":"tool_result","content":"**Config**\n- Env var: `MIN_CLIENT_VERSION`\n- Config key: `app.min_client_version` in `config/app.php`, set to `env('MIN_CLIENT_VERSION')`.\n- Default: `null`, so the check is off. The config comment says \"null turns the check off.\"\n\n**Middleware** (`RecordClientVersion`, extended, not a new middleware)\n- **Header:** `X-Client-Version`, compared against the existing `PATTERN` constant. The diff doesn't show that constant's regex.\n- **When it runs:** before `$next`, so it applies even to requests that would otherwise fail authentication.\n- **Which routes:** only routes whose middleware includes `auth:sanctum`. Per the implementation notes, this covers all of that group, including `auth/logout`, `refresh`, `tokens`, `revoke-token` and `passkeys/*`. `health` and `auth/login` are not affected.\n- **Comparison:** `version_compare($header, $min, '<')`, so the check is numeric per part. `1.0.9` is below `1.0.10`.\n\n**Rejection response**\n- HTTP status 426, built with `ApiResponse::error`.\n- Message: \"Please update the app.\"\n- `meta.min_client_version` contains the configured minimum.\n\n**Unset, empty, or missing values**\n- **Unset env var:** the config value is `null`, and the check is skipped.\n- **Empty string:** also skipped, because the code returns false when the minimum is not a non-empty string.\n- **Missing header:** allowed (200).\n- **Invalid header** (e.g. `abc`): treated as missing and allowed.\n\n**Tests** (`ClientMinimumVersionTest.php`)\n- Check off: allowed.\n- `1.0.9` against `1.0.10`: 426 with the envelope and meta.\n- Equal and above: allowed.\n- Missing and invalid headers: allowed.\n- `health` and `auth/login` with an old header: allowed.\n\n**Open points noted in the diff**\n- Authenticated `auth/*` routes (e.g. logout, refresh) are blocked below the minimum, which may conflict with the brief. The owner needs to confirm this.\n- An outdated request with no or invalid token gets 426 rather than 401."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3d69f9c-a2d3-42af-8038-53845031b34c","uuid":"24f63226-e855-473f-8b77-c77a6841ecfe","timestamp":"2026-10-14T20:34:17.559Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":924522,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Config**\n- Env var: `MIN_CLIENT_VERSION`\n- Config key: `app.min_client_version` in `config/app.php`, set to `env('MIN_CLIENT_VERSION')`.\n- Default: `null`, so the check is off. The config comment says \"null turns the check off.\"\n\n**Middleware** (`RecordClientVersion`, extended, not a new middleware)\n- **Header:** `X-Client-Version`, compared against the existing `PATTERN` constant. The diff doesn't show that constant's regex.\n- **When it runs:** before `$next`, so it applies even to requests that would otherwise fail authentication.\n- **Which routes:** only routes whose middleware includes `auth:sanctum`. Per the implementation notes, this covers all of that group, including `auth/logout`, `refresh`, `tokens`, `revoke-token` and `passkeys/*`. `health` and `auth/login` are not affected.\n- **Comparison:** `version_compare($header, $min, '<')`, so the check is numeric per part. `1.0.9` is below `1.0.10`.\n\n**Rejection response**\n- HTTP status 426, built with `ApiResponse::error`.\n- Message: \"Please update the app.\"\n- `meta.min_client_version` contains the configured minimum.\n\n**Unset, empty, or missing values**\n- **Unset env var:** the config value is `null`, and the check is skipped.\n- **Empty string:** also skipped, because the code returns false when the minimum is not a non-empty string.\n- **Missing header:** allowed (200).\n- **Invalid header** (e.g. `abc`): treated as missing and allowed.\n\n**Tests** (`ClientMinimumVersionTest.php`)\n- Check off: allowed.\n- `1.0.9` against `1.0.10`: 426 with the envelope and meta.\n- Equal and above: allowed.\n- Missing and invalid headers: allowed.\n- `health` and `auth/login` with an old header: allowed.\n\n**Open points noted in the diff**\n- Authenticated `auth/*` routes (e.g. logout, refresh) are blocked below the minimum, which may conflict with the brief. The owner needs to confirm this.\n- An outdated request with no or invalid token gets 426 rather than 401.","durationMs":7881,"url":"https://github.com/solyto/api/commit/c5f3b99"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0125UjFUF2ygL5m93Dgy46DT","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T8Ay8oQA53CcTsSnPMkYx7","type":"tool_result","content":"**Env vars (both optional, read only in `config/services.php`)**\n- `API_TRAFFIC_ALERT_THRESHOLD`, default `300`, cast to int, stored as `services.traffic.alert_threshold`.\n- `API_TRAFFIC_ALERT_COOLDOWN`, default `3600` seconds, cast to int, stored as `services.traffic.alert_cooldown`.\n- The `traffic` log channel also reads `LOG_LEVEL` (default `debug`).\n- ntfy uses the existing `services.ntfy.url`, `topic`, and `token` settings. The diff adds no new ntfy variables.\n\n**Alert delivery**\n- **ntfy only.** The notification uses `NtfyChannel` with the configured topic. The diff contains no mail or Telegram channels.\n- **Log file.** Each alert also writes to `storage/logs/traffic.log` through a new single-file `traffic` channel.\n- The notification has a title of \"High API traffic\" and a message stating the user ID and the request count within one minute. It contains no email or name.\n- The job runs once (`$tries = 1`) with a 30-second timeout. A failed send is not retried.\n\n**What goes into traffic.log**\n- One warning per alert, with the message \"API traffic threshold exceeded\".\n- Context fields: `user_id`, `count`, and `route` (the route name, or the URI pattern if unnamed).\n\n**Scope and timing**\n- **Per user.** Each user has their own counter (`api-traffic:{userId}`) and their own alert flag (`api-traffic-alerted:{userId}`).\n- **Per 60-second window.** Requests are counted with `RateLimiter::hit` over a 60-second window.\n- **Alert trigger.** An alert fires when the count exceeds the threshold and no alert has been sent for that user within the cooldown.\n- **Cooldown.** Once an alert is sent, further alerts for that user are suppressed for the cooldown period. The log entry follows the same gate, so each alert produces exactly one log line.\n- **Authenticated only.** Unauthenticated requests are not counted.\n- **Observe only.** The middleware never blocks or slows a request."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3d69f9c-a2d3-42af-8038-53845031b34c","uuid":"435432e0-009a-4050-af7b-4c7228a38a83","timestamp":"2026-10-14T20:34:19.430Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":881643,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"**Env vars (both optional, read only in `config/services.php`)**\n- `API_TRAFFIC_ALERT_THRESHOLD`, default `300`, cast to int, stored as `services.traffic.alert_threshold`.\n- `API_TRAFFIC_ALERT_COOLDOWN`, default `3600` seconds, cast to int, stored as `services.traffic.alert_cooldown`.\n- The `traffic` log channel also reads `LOG_LEVEL` (default `debug`).\n- ntfy uses the existing `services.ntfy.url`, `topic`, and `token` settings. The diff adds no new ntfy variables.\n\n**Alert delivery**\n- **ntfy only.** The notification uses `NtfyChannel` with the configured topic. The diff contains no mail or Telegram channels.\n- **Log file.** Each alert also writes to `storage/logs/traffic.log` through a new single-file `traffic` channel.\n- The notification has a title of \"High API traffic\" and a message stating the user ID and the request count within one minute. It contains no email or name.\n- The job runs once (`$tries = 1`) with a 30-second timeout. A failed send is not retried.\n\n**What goes into traffic.log**\n- One warning per alert, with the message \"API traffic threshold exceeded\".\n- Context fields: `user_id`, `count`, and `route` (the route name, or the URI pattern if unnamed).\n\n**Scope and timing**\n- **Per user.** Each user has their own counter (`api-traffic:{userId}`) and their own alert flag (`api-traffic-alerted:{userId}`).\n- **Per 60-second window.** Requests are counted with `RateLimiter::hit` over a 60-second window.\n- **Alert trigger.** An alert fires when the count exceeds the threshold and no alert has been sent for that user within the cooldown.\n- **Cooldown.** Once an alert is sent, further alerts for that user are suppressed for the cooldown period. The log entry follows the same gate, so each alert produces exactly one log line.\n- **Authenticated only.** Unauthenticated requests are not counted.\n- **Observe only.** The middleware never blocks or slows a request.","durationMs":10640,"url":"https://github.com/solyto/api/commit/fb9b5d1"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01T8Ay8oQA53CcTsSnPMkYx7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
